---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="A coding agent taking shape in V"
  description="Veasel Code is an open-source coding agent built around a native V runtime, a local API, and durable sessions."
>
  <section class="hero page-grid">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        <span class="signal"></span> V-native coding agent · early development
      </p>
      <h1>
        Make the machine
        <br />
        show its <em>work.</em>
      </h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Veasel Code is taking shape around one clear idea: an agent should be
        inspectable, resumable, and close to the code it changes.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a
          class="button button-primary"
          href="https://github.com/veasel-labs/veasel"
        >
          Explore the source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
        <a class="text-link" href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/`}>
          Read the field guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="status-note">
        <span class="status-dot"></span> Foundation slice running locally ·
        model execution is next
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="trace-card" aria-label="Session lifecycle illustration">
      <div class="trace-top">
        <span>SESSION / 0001</span>
        <span class="trace-live">● LOCAL</span>
      </div>
      <div class="trace-row">
        <span class="trace-index">01</span>
        <span class="trace-node node-done">●</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Workspace opened</strong>
          <small>repo context attached</small>
        </div>
        <span class="trace-tag">READY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="trace-row">
        <span class="trace-index">02</span>
        <span class="trace-node node-active">◉</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Task queued</strong>
          <small>durable session event</small>
        </div>
        <span class="trace-tag tag-active">SAVED</span>
      </div>
      <div class="trace-row trace-muted">
        <span class="trace-index">03</span>
        <span class="trace-node">○</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Agent response</strong>
          <small>provider integration in progress</small>
        </div>
        <span class="trace-tag">NEXT</span>
      </div>
      <div class="trace-bottom">
        <span>EVENT STREAM</span>
        <span>REPLAYABLE ↻</span>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-stamp" aria-hidden="true">
      FIELD
      <br />
      NOTES
      <br />
      <b>001</b>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="principles page-grid" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
    <div class="section-label">
      <span>01 / PRINCIPLES</span>
      <span>THE WORKING THEORY</span>
    </div>
    <h2 id="principles-title">
      An agent you can
      <br />
      <em>follow through.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="principle-list">
      <article>
        <span class="principle-no">A</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Local by default</h3>
          <p>
            The backend binds to loopback. Sessions live in SQLite on your
            machine.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="principle-no">B</span>
        <div>
          <h3>State that survives</h3>
          <p>
            Session changes and their events commit together, ready to replay
            after reconnect.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="principle-no">C</span>
        <div>
          <h3>V at the core</h3>
          <p>
            Transport, persistence, and the future agent runtime are implemented
            in V.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="readout page-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">CURRENT BUILD / 0.1</p>
      <h2>
        A solid floor
        <br />
        before the tall walls.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="readout-copy">
      <p>
        The first slice establishes a real API, transactional session storage,
        server-sent event replay, and a keyboard-first terminal client. No model
        response is faked while the runtime is still being built.
      </p>
      <a
        class="text-link"
        href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/architecture/`}
      >
        See how the pieces fit <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
